\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {III.10}{\ignorespaces Identification of the source origins of the INPs active at \SI {-20}{\degreeCelsius } and observed during the MOCCHA campaign. The detection uses the improved ratio method. Panel A is the raw ratio of the \SI {10}{\percent } highest observed concentrations. Panel B is the raw ratio of the \SI {33}{\percent } lowest observed concentrations. Yellow to red indicate detection signal, while the blueish colour means no signal. Panel C is the composite ratio (c.f. \cref  {P1sec:improved_method}), the actual identification results. Panel D is the time series of INP concentrations measured during the campaign for four activation temperatures.}}{82}{figure.caption.42}\protected@file@percent }
